---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CHANNELS, REACH_OUT, utm } from "../lib/course";
---

<Base
  title="About | AIR Course 001"
  description="Who is behind AIR Course 001, why the course exists, and what to reach out about."
  pageSlug="about"
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="section measure">
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>
      <h1>Quality among noise</h1>

      <p>
        Course 001 is written by Kranthi Manchikanti, a solutions architect working on agentic
        systems in regulated and healthcare settings, and the person behind
        <a href={CHANNELS.publication} rel="noopener">The AI Runtime</a>: a publication, a Boston
        meetup, a public engineering lab, and the FDE Talks podcast.
      </p>

      <p>
        This course exists because the gap in agent education is not model knowledge. It is
        runtime knowledge. There is no shortage of tutorials that get an agent working once,
        and very little written about what happens when the process dies at step nine, when the
        publish call times out after it already succeeded, or when a reviewer approves three
        hours later from their phone. Those are the parts that decide whether an agent ships.
      </p>

      <p>
        The role it trains is the <strong>Forward Deployed Engineer</strong>. An FDE ships an
        agent into someone else's production reality, is accountable for it running next week,
        and has to answer "what happens after failure" in the customer's conference room with
        evidence rather than confidence. Every module ends with an invariant you can prove,
        because that is the currency of the job.
      </p>

      <p>
        Everything here is free and public: the written curriculum, the fixture server, the
        golden datasets, the evaluators, and the Field Reports. Public artifacts are the point.
        Claims about reliability are only worth something if a stranger can reproduce them, so
        every Failure Lab runs against a deterministic fixture server and every eval ships with
        its labels.
      </p>

      <h2>What this course is not</h2>
      <p>
        Not a platform, not an LMS, not a cohort you buy. No accounts, no progress tracking, no
        paywall, no comments. If you want the artifacts as they ship, subscribe to the
        newsletter. That is the only ask on the whole site.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <ul class="contact">
        <li>
          <span class="contact__key">EMAIL</span>
          <a href={CHANNELS.email}>info@theairuntime.com</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="contact__key">LINKEDIN</span>
          <a href={CHANNELS.linkedin} rel="noopener">Kranthi Manchikanti</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="contact__key">SUBSTACK</span>
          <a href={utm(CHANNELS.substack, "about", "subscribe")} rel="noopener">theairuntime.com</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="contact__key">PODCAST</span>
          <a href={utm(CHANNELS.podcast, "about", "listen")} rel="noopener">FDE Talks</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="contact__key">LAB</span>
          <a href={CHANNELS.lab} rel="noopener">lab.theairuntime.com</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="contact__key">EVENTS</span>
          <a href={CHANNELS.events} rel="noopener">events.theairuntime.com</a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="reach">{REACH_OUT}</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .contact {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .contact li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
  }
  .contact__key {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    width: 7rem;
    flex: none;
  }
  .reach {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--t-meta);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }
</style>
